{
     "role": "tool",
     "tool_call_id": "call_AbCd123",
     "content": "{\"error\": \"CIRCUIT_BREAKER_TRIPPED: Identical call has failed 2 times consecutively. Further executions of this tool with these parameters are blocked. Please formulate an alternative strategy or report the blocking condition to the user.\"}"
   }
   ```
4. **Exponential Backoff with Jitter for Remote MCP Calls**: When connecting to remote MCP servers over HTTP/SSE or WebSocket, network blips and transient server reboots must not crash active reasoning sessions. The bridge client implements truncated exponential backoff with full jitter:
   $T_{\text{backoff}} = \min(T_{\text{max}}, T_{\text{base}} \times 2^{\text{attempt}}) \times \text{Uniform}(0, 1)$
   This ensures that concurrent agent instances reconnecting after a network partition do not inadvertently launch a distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) thundering herd attack against the MCP gateway.


## 6.5 Cross-Vendor Agent Adapter Architecture: Unifying OpenAI, Claude & Gemini

Enterprise platforms rarely standardize on a single foundation model forever. An organization may deploy GPT-4o for high-throughput customer support, Claude 3.5 Sonnet for complex coding and analytical synthesis, and Gemini 1.5 Pro for massive multi-million-token document digestion.

Building separate tool integrations for each vendor results in code duplication and operational fragility. The **Cross-Vendor MCP Adapter** abstracts model-specific nuances, presenting a single, unified interface.

